---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Give It to Me — Daf Yomi Game: Bekhorot 26"
  description="Bekhorot 26: run a firstborn nursery while a kohen knocks at the gate asking for the animal too early, rebuild Rava's three disputes over a firstborn's shed wool, find the one tanna who fits the dangling-wool mishna, press a fleece to see which strands stick out, and sort Rabbi Yannai's offerings."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;500;700;900&display=swap"
  />

  <main class="frank min-h-screen bg-[#16130e] !text-[#efe7d6]">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <header class="px-4 pt-12 pb-8">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-sm !text-[#a59a83]">
          <a href="/daf" class="underline decoration-[#4a4232] hover:!text-[#d9b45a]">Daf Yomi Arcade</a>, Bekhorot 26, 14 October 2026
        </p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-5xl font-black leading-[1.05] sm:text-6xl">Give It to Me</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-2xl !text-[#d9b45a]" dir="rtl" lang="he">אָמַר לוֹ הַכֹּהֵן בְּתוֹךְ הַזְּמַן ״תְּנֵהוּ לִי״</p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed !text-[#d6ccb6]">
          A firstborn lamb belongs to the kohen, but the owner has to raise it first: thirty days for a lamb, fifty for a calf.
          What if the kohen turns up early and says “give it to me”? Today you run the nursery. Then the daf goes back to the
          firstborn’s wool: what about hair that falls out before the animal is slaughtered, and strands still dangling
          when it’s shorn?
        </p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 600 120" class="mt-6 w-full" aria-hidden="true">
          <rect x="0" y="96" width="600" height="24" fill="#2a2318" />
          <g stroke="#7a6542" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round">
            <line x1="40" y1="50" x2="40" y2="100" /><line x1="140" y1="50" x2="140" y2="100" />
            <line x1="240" y1="50" x2="240" y2="100" /><line x1="340" y1="50" x2="340" y2="100" />
            <line x1="30" y1="62" x2="350" y2="62" /><line x1="30" y1="82" x2="350" y2="82" />
          </g>
          <g transform="translate(180 64)">
            <ellipse cx="0" cy="18" rx="30" ry="18" fill="#efe7d6" />
            <circle cx="-14" cy="10" r="10" fill="#efe7d6" /><circle cx="8" cy="6" r="11" fill="#efe7d6" />
            <circle cx="24" cy="8" r="9" fill="#2a2318" /><rect x="-16" y="30" width="5" height="10" fill="#2a2318" /><rect x="14" y="30" width="5" height="10" fill="#2a2318" />
          </g>
          <g transform="translate(440 30)">
            <rect x="-6" y="0" width="70" height="70" rx="4" fill="#3a3122" stroke="#7a6542" stroke-width="3" />
            <circle cx="30" cy="38" r="3" fill="#d9b45a" />
            <text x="96" y="30" font-size="15" fill="#d9b45a" font-family="Frank Ruhl Libre, serif">knock</text>
            <text x="106" y="52" font-size="15" fill="#d9b45a" font-family="Frank Ruhl Libre, serif">knock</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-sm">
          <span class="rounded-full border border-[#4a4232] px-3 py-1 !text-[#d6ccb6]">Score <b id="score" class="!text-[#d9b45a]">0</b></span>
          <span class="!text-[#a59a83]">Six stations, about 10 minutes. Every case links to its line on Sefaria.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- ============ 1. Nursery calendar ============ -->
    <section class="px-4 py-10 border-t border-[#2e2719]">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#8fae7a]">Station 1 · The nursery calendar</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">The kohen at the gate</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed !text-[#d6ccb6]">
          The days tick by in the pen. When the kohen knocks, decide: hand the firstborn over, or keep tending it.
          The mishna (<a class="link" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.26b.8">26b:8</a>): small animals thirty days,
          large animals fifty; Rabbi Yosei says three months for small ones.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-[#3a3122] bg-[#1d1912] p-4 sm:p-5">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-sm !text-[#a59a83]">
            <span id="nc-progress">Case 1 of 7</span>
            <span id="nc-animal" class="text-2xl" aria-hidden="true">🐑</span>
          </div>
          <svg id="nc-strip" viewBox="0 0 600 70" class="mt-3 w-full" role="img" aria-label="Day strip">
            <rect x="20" y="30" width="560" height="10" rx="5" fill="#2e2719" />
            <rect id="nc-fill" x="20" y="30" width="0" height="10" rx="5" fill="#8fae7a" />
            <g id="nc-flags"></g>
            <circle id="nc-dot" cx="20" cy="35" r="9" fill="#efe7d6" stroke="#16130e" stroke-width="2" />
            <text id="nc-day" x="20" y="64" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle" fill="#efe7d6" font-family="Frank Ruhl Libre, serif">day 0</text>
          </svg>
          <div id="nc-card" class="mt-3" aria-live="polite"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 2. Year clock ============ -->
    <section class="px-4 py-10 border-t border-[#2e2719]">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#8fae7a]">Station 2 · Year by year</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">How long may I keep it?</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed !text-[#d6ccb6]" dir="rtl" lang="he">
          הַבְּכוֹר נֶאֱכָל שָׁנָה בְּשָׁנָה, בֵּין תָּם בֵּין בַּעַל מוּם
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#d6ccb6]">
          “You shall eat it before the Lord your God year by year” (Deut. 15:20). Today a blemished firstborn is in your
          care. When the blemish appears decides how long you may keep it before eating it
          (<a class="link" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.26b.9">26b:9</a>).
        </p>
        <div id="yc" class="mt-6 space-y-4"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 3. Rava's three disputes ============ -->
    <section class="px-4 py-10 border-t border-[#2e2719]">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#8fae7a]">Station 3 · Rava’s board</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">Three disputes over one window</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed !text-[#d6ccb6]">
          A blemished firstborn sheds some wool (or someone plucks it), and the owner puts it away in a compartment
          (<span dir="rtl" lang="he">חַלּוֹן</span>). Later the animal is either <b>slaughtered</b> or simply <b>dies</b>.
          May he use the wool? Akavya ben Mahalalel permits and the Rabbis forbid, but <i>where</i> do they disagree?
          Rava says three tannaim give three different answers
          (<a class="link" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.26a.6-7">26a:6–7</a>). Fill in each cell.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full min-w-[460px] border-separate border-spacing-2 text-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-normal !text-[#a59a83]"></th>
                <th class="text-left font-bold !text-[#efe7d6]">Slaughtered 🔪</th>
                <th class="text-left font-bold !text-[#efe7d6]">Died 🪦</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="rv-body"></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs !text-[#a59a83]">Tap a cell to cycle: Disputed → All permit → All forbid.</p>
        <button id="rv-check" class="btn mt-4">Check the board</button>
        <div id="rv-out" class="mt-4" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 4. Whose mishna ============ -->
    <section class="px-4 py-10 border-t border-[#2e2719]">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#8fae7a]">Station 4 · Rav Naḥman bar Yitzḥak’s lineup</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">Who wrote the dangling-wool clause?</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed !text-[#d6ccb6]">
          Rav Naḥman rules like Rabbi Yehuda, because the mishna in Eduyot 5:6 matches him
          (<a class="link" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.26a.8">26a:8</a>). Rav Naḥman bar Yitzḥak adds a proof from the
          mishna’s next line: dangling wool on a firstborn shorn after its death
          <b>is permitted if it looks like part of the fleece</b> and <b>forbidden if it doesn’t</b>. So some opinion has to give
          those two kinds of wool <i>different</i> rulings. Test each suspect: Fits, or Doesn’t fit?
          (<a class="link" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.26a.9-13">26a:9–13</a>)
        </p>
        <div id="sus" class="mt-6 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2"></div>
        <div id="sus-out" class="mt-4" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 5. Fleece press ============ -->
    <section class="px-4 py-10 border-t border-[#2e2719]">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#8fae7a]">Station 5 · The fleece press</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">Which strands aren’t “part of the fleece”?</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed !text-[#d6ccb6]" dir="rtl" lang="he">
          כֹּל שֶׁעִיקָּרוֹ הָפוּךְ כְּלַפֵּי רֹאשׁוֹ · כֹּל שֶׁאֵינוֹ מִתְמַעֵךְ עִם הַגִּיזָּה
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#d6ccb6]">
          Reish Lakish: a strand whose <b>root is turned outward</b>, toward its tip. Rav Natan bar Oshaya: a strand that
          <b>doesn’t press down</b> with the rest of the fleece
          (<a class="link" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.26b.5">26b:5</a>). Use the press to find the springy strands,
          then tap every strand that is forbidden under the opinion shown.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-[#3a3122] bg-[#1d1912] p-4">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
            <p class="text-sm"><span class="!text-[#a59a83]">Ruling by:</span> <b id="fl-lens" class="!text-[#d9b45a]">Reish Lakish</b></p>
            <button id="fl-press" class="btn-ghost">Press the fleece ⤓</button>
          </div>
          <svg id="fl-svg" viewBox="0 0 600 220" class="mt-3 w-full touch-manipulation" role="group" aria-label="Fleece with strands"></svg>
          <p class="text-xs !text-[#a59a83]">A gold dot marks a strand’s root. Tap (or Tab + Enter) a strand to mark it forbidden.</p>
          <button id="fl-check" class="btn mt-3">Check these strands</button>
          <div id="fl-out" class="mt-3" aria-live="polite"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 6. Yannai's shelf ============ -->
    <section class="px-4 py-10 border-t border-[#2e2719]">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#8fae7a]">Station 6 · Rabbi Yannai’s shelf</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">Wool that fell out on its own</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed !text-[#d6ccb6]">
          Wool came loose <i>by itself</i> from an unblemished consecrated animal that was later slaughtered. Nobody would
          permit wool someone <i>plucked</i> on purpose. But wool that just fell? The Gemara says it depends on whether the
          owner is tempted to <b>keep the animal around</b> (and shear or work it)
          (<a class="link" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.26a.14-26b.1">26a:14–26b:1</a>). Shelve each offering.
        </p>
        <div id="yn" class="mt-6 space-y-3"></div>
        <div id="yn-proof" class="mt-6"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 7. Threshing floor ============ -->
    <section class="px-4 py-10 border-t border-[#2e2719]">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#8fae7a]">Coda · The helper at the threshing floor</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">Why not hand it over early?</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed !text-[#d6ccb6]">
          Rav Sheshet: a kohen who takes the firstborn early saves the owner the work of raising it, so he looks like
          <span dir="rtl" lang="he">כֹּהֵן הַמְסַיֵּיעַ בְּבֵית הַגֳּרָנוֹת</span>, a kohen who helps at the threshing floor to get the
          teruma (<a class="link" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.26b.17-21">26b:17–21</a>). The baraita about those helpers:
        </p>
        <div id="tf" class="mt-6 space-y-4"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ Finale ============ -->
    <section class="px-4 py-10 border-t border-[#2e2719]">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <div id="final" class="rounded-xl border border-[#4a4232] bg-[#1d1912] p-5">
          <p class="text-sm !text-[#a59a83]">Your nursery ledger</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-3xl font-black"><span id="final-score" class="!text-[#d9b45a]">0</span> <span class="text-lg !text-[#a59a83]">/ <span id="final-max">0</span></span></p>
          <p id="final-title" class="mt-2 !text-[#d6ccb6]">Play the stations above to fill the ledger.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ Learn the real daf ============ -->
    <section class="px-4 py-12 border-t border-[#2e2719]">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Learn the real daf</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed !text-[#d6ccb6]">
          The game is a door, not a replacement. Bekhorot 26 finishes the wool sugya (Akavya ben Mahalalel and the Rabbis,
          Rava’s three disputes, Rabbi Yannai’s unresolved burnt-offering question), then opens a new mishna on how long the
          owner raises the firstborn, with Rav Kahana’s and Rava’s readings of Exodus 22:28–29 for the thirty and fifty days.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2">
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.26a" class="link">Bekhorot 26a on Sefaria</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.26b" class="link">Bekhorot 26b on Sefaria</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Bekhorot.26a" class="link">Rashi (48 comments)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Gershom_on_Bekhorot.26a" class="link">Rabbeinu Gershom (48)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Steinsaltz_on_Bekhorot.26a" class="link">Steinsaltz (35)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Bekhorot.26a" class="link">Tosafot (8)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Eduyot.5.6" class="link">Mishnah Eduyot 5:6</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Exodus.22.28-29" class="link">Exodus 22:28–29</a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm"><a href="/daf" class="link">← Back to the Daf Yomi Arcade</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <style>
    .frank { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', 'David', serif; }
    .link { color: #d9b45a !important; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: #6b5a36; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
    .link:hover { color: #efe7d6 !important; }
    .btn { background: #d9b45a; color: #16130e !important; font-weight: 700; padding: 0.55rem 1.1rem; border-radius: 0.6rem; }
    .btn:hover { background: #e8c672; }
    .btn-ghost { border: 1px solid #6b5a36; color: #efe7d6 !important; padding: 0.45rem 0.9rem; border-radius: 0.6rem; }
    .btn-ghost:hover { border-color: #d9b45a; }
    .chip { border: 1px solid #4a4232; border-radius: 0.6rem; padding: 0.5rem 0.8rem; text-align: left; color: #efe7d6 !important; background: #211c14; }
    .chip:hover:not(:disabled) { border-color: #d9b45a; }
    .chip:disabled { opacity: 0.85; cursor: default; }
    .chip.good { border-color: #8fae7a; background: #1f2a1a; }
    .chip.bad { border-color: #c0664a; background: #2d1a14; }
    button:focus-visible, [tabindex]:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #d9b45a; outline-offset: 2px; }
    .note { border-left: 3px solid #8fae7a; padding: 0.5rem 0.9rem; background: #1b2117; border-radius: 0 0.5rem 0.5rem 0; }
    .note.miss { border-left-color: #c0664a; background: #241713; }
    .strand { cursor: pointer; transition: transform 0.6s ease; transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: bottom; }
    .pressed .strand.flat { transform: scaleY(0.35); }
    .press-plate { transition: transform 0.6s ease; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .strand, .press-plate { transition: none !important; }
    }
  </style>

  <script is:inline>
    (() => {
      const reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
      const S = 'https://www.sefaria.org/';
      let score = 0, max = 0;
      const addMax = (n) => { max += n; $('final-max').textContent = max; };
      const award = (n) => {
        score += n; $('score').textContent = score; $('final-score').textContent = score;
        const pct = score / max;
        $('final-title').textContent =
          pct >= 0.9 ? 'Faithful shepherd: you raised every firstborn to the day and kept every strand straight.' :
          pct >= 0.65 ? 'Good tending. A few strands got loose in the press.' :
          pct >= 0.35 ? 'The kohen is still knocking. Go back through the daf and try again.' :
          'Keep tending: the daf is waiting on Sefaria.';
      };
      const note = (ok, html) => `<div class="note ${ok ? '' : 'miss'} mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#efe7d6]">${html}</div>`;
      const ref = (r, label) => `<a class="link" href="${S}${r}">${label}</a>`;

      /* ---------- 1. Nursery calendar ---------- */
      const SCALE = 100; // days shown on strip
      const xOf = (d) => 20 + (Math.min(d, SCALE) / SCALE) * 560;
      const kinds = {
        lamb: { icon: '🐑', he: 'דַּקָּה', label: 'lamb (small animal)' },
        kid: { icon: '🐐', he: 'דַּקָּה', label: 'kid (small animal)' },
        calf: { icon: '🐄', he: 'גַּסָּה', label: 'calf (large animal)' },
      };
      const NC = [
        { kind: 'lamb', day: 12, lens: 'the first tanna', ask: '“Give it to me.”', blem: false, temple: false,
          ans: 'keep', why: [
            ['It would look like the kohen is being paid for helping, like a kohen at the threshing floor', true],
            ['A twelve-day-old lamb may not be eaten', false],
            ['Firstborns may only be given on a festival', false]],
          expl: 'Thirty days for a small animal. Inside that window the owner may not hand it over. Rav Sheshet: the kohen saves the owner the work of raising it, so it looks like a kohen “helping at the threshing floor” to earn his gifts (26b:17).',
          r: 'Bekhorot.26b.17' },
        { kind: 'calf', day: 38, lens: 'the first tanna', ask: '“Give it to me.”', blem: false, temple: false,
          ans: 'keep', expl: 'A large animal needs fifty days. Day 38 is still inside the window. Rava: “So you shall do with your oxen” adds an extra act of doing for oxen, and the Sages set the extra time at fifty (26b:13–14).',
          r: 'Bekhorot.26b.13-14' },
        { kind: 'calf', day: 52, lens: 'the first tanna', ask: '“Give it to me.”', blem: false, temple: false,
          ans: 'give', expl: 'Fifty days are done. The owner has finished the tending the Torah asked of him, so he can give the calf to the kohen.',
          r: 'Bekhorot.26b.8' },
        { kind: 'lamb', day: 45, lens: 'the first tanna', ask: '“Give it to me.”', blem: false, temple: false,
          ans: 'give', expl: 'For the first tanna a small animal needs only thirty days, so day 45 is past the window. Next: the same lamb, ruled by Rabbi Yosei.',
          r: 'Bekhorot.26b.8' },
        { kind: 'lamb', day: 45, lens: 'Rabbi Yosei', ask: '“Give it to me.”', blem: false, temple: false,
          ans: 'keep', expl: 'Rabbi Yosei: three months for a small animal, “because its tending is extensive”. A tanna explained that a lamb’s teeth are small and it can’t eat most foods (26b:16).',
          r: 'Bekhorot.26b.16' },
        { kind: 'kid', day: 9, lens: 'the mishna', ask: '“Give it to me so I may eat it.”', blem: true, temple: false,
          ans: 'give', expl: 'A blemished firstborn that the kohen wants to eat now: the mishna permits it. There’s nothing left to raise it for (26b:8).',
          r: 'Bekhorot.26b.8' },
        { kind: 'lamb', day: 20, lens: 'the mishna', ask: '“Give it to me and I will sacrifice it.”', blem: false, temple: true,
          ans: 'give', expl: 'When the Temple stands and the firstborn is unblemished, a kohen who wants to offer it now may take it. It is going straight to the altar, not to be raised by the kohen (26b:8).',
          r: 'Bekhorot.26b.8' },
      ];
      NC.forEach((c) => addMax(c.why ? 2 : 1));
      let ncI = 0, ncAnim = 0;
      const drawFlags = (c) => {
        const flags = [
          { d: 30, t: '30', on: c.kind !== 'calf' && c.lens !== 'Rabbi Yosei' },
          { d: 50, t: '50', on: c.kind === 'calf' },
          { d: 90, t: '3 mo', on: c.kind !== 'calf' && c.lens === 'Rabbi Yosei' },
        ];
        $('nc-flags').innerHTML = flags.map((f) => `
          <g opacity="${f.on ? 1 : 0.3}">
            <line x1="${xOf(f.d)}" y1="10" x2="${xOf(f.d)}" y2="44" stroke="${f.on ? '#d9b45a' : '#6b5a36'}" stroke-width="2" />
            <text x="${xOf(f.d)}" y="8" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" fill="${f.on ? '#d9b45a' : '#a59a83'}" font-family="Frank Ruhl Libre, serif">${f.t}</text>
          </g>`).join('');
      };
      const setDay = (d) => {
        const x = xOf(d);
        $('nc-dot').setAttribute('cx', x); $('nc-fill').setAttribute('width', x - 20);
        $('nc-day').setAttribute('x', x); $('nc-day').textContent = `day ${Math.round(d)}`;
      };
      const runTo = (target, done) => {
        cancelAnimationFrame(ncAnim);
        if (reduce) { setDay(target); done(); return; }
        const t0 = performance.now(), dur = 900;
        const step = (t) => {
          const p = Math.min(1, (t - t0) / dur);
          setDay(target * (1 - Math.pow(1 - p, 3)));
          if (p < 1) ncAnim = requestAnimationFrame(step); else done();
        };
        ncAnim = requestAnimationFrame(step);
      };
      const ncShow = () => {
        if (ncI >= NC.length) {
          $('nc-progress').textContent = 'Nursery closed';
          $('nc-card').innerHTML = note(true, 'All seven knocks answered. Where do thirty and fifty come from? Rav Kahana tried pairing Exodus 22:28 with 22:29 (firstborn sons at thirty days → sheep; first fruits at Shavuot, fifty days → oxen), but you could pair them the other way round. Rava: both animals follow the firstborn son’s thirty, and “so you shall <i>do</i> with your oxen” adds more for oxen. The Sages fixed that at fifty. ' + ref('Bekhorot.26b.10-15', '26b:10–15'));
          return;
        }
        const c = NC[ncI], k = kinds[c.kind];
        $('nc-progress').textContent = `Case ${ncI + 1} of ${NC.length}`;
        $('nc-animal').textContent = k.icon;
        drawFlags(c); setDay(0);
        $('nc-card').innerHTML = `<p class="text-sm !text-[#a59a83]">Raising a firstborn ${k.label} · <span dir="rtl" lang="he">${k.he}</span>${c.blem ? ' · <b class="!text-[#c0664a]">blemished</b>' : ' · unblemished'}${c.temple ? ' · <b class="!text-[#d9b45a]">Temple standing</b>' : ''}</p>`;
        runTo(c.day, () => {
          $('nc-card').innerHTML += `
            <p class="mt-3 text-lg">🚪 <b>Knock knock.</b> The kohen: <span class="!text-[#d9b45a]">${c.ask}</span></p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm !text-[#a59a83]">Rule according to <b class="!text-[#efe7d6]">${c.lens}</b>.</p>
            <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              <button class="chip" data-a="give">Hand it over</button>
              <button class="chip" data-a="keep">Not yet: keep tending</button>
            </div><div id="nc-fb"></div>`;
          $('nc-card').querySelectorAll('[data-a]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => ncAnswer(b)));
        });
      };
      const ncNext = () => `<button class="btn mt-3" id="nc-next">${ncI + 1 < NC.length ? 'Next day in the pen →' : 'Close the nursery'}</button>`;
      const ncAnswer = (b) => {
        const c = NC[ncI];
        const ok = b.dataset.a === c.ans;
        $('nc-card').querySelectorAll('[data-a]').forEach((x) => { x.disabled = true; if (x.dataset.a === c.ans) x.classList.add('good'); });
        if (!ok) b.classList.add('bad'); else award(1);
        const body = `${ok ? 'Right.' : 'Not quite.'} ${c.expl} ${ref(c.r, 'Source')}`;
        if (c.why) {
          $('nc-fb').innerHTML = note(ok, body) + `<p class="mt-3 text-sm">Why may he not give it early?</p><div class="mt-2 grid gap-2">${c.why.map((w, i) => `<button class="chip text-sm" data-w="${i}">${w[0]}</button>`).join('')}</div><div id="nc-fb2"></div>`;
          $('nc-fb').querySelectorAll('[data-w]').forEach((wb) => wb.addEventListener('click', () => {
            const good = c.why[+wb.dataset.w][1];
            $('nc-fb').querySelectorAll('[data-w]').forEach((x) => { x.disabled = true; if (c.why[+x.dataset.w][1]) x.classList.add('good'); });
            if (!good) wb.classList.add('bad'); else award(1);
            $('nc-fb2').innerHTML = note(good, 'Rav Sheshet: he looks like a kohen who helps at the threshing floor to get teruma. The free labor works like payment for the gift. (See the coda below.)') + ncNext();
            $('nc-next').addEventListener('click', () => { ncI++; ncShow(); });
          }));
        } else {
          $('nc-fb').innerHTML = note(ok, body) + ncNext();
          $('nc-next').addEventListener('click', () => { ncI++; ncShow(); });
        }
      };
      ncShow();

      /* ---------- 2. Year clock ---------- */
      const YC = [
        { q: 'The blemish appears in its <b>7th month</b>. Until when may you keep it?', opts: ['30 days from the blemish', 'Until the end of its first twelve months', 'Only until the expert sees it'], a: 1,
          e: 'A blemish inside its first year: you may keep it for the whole twelve months. “Year by year” gives it its first year.' },
        { q: 'The blemish appears in its <b>14th month</b>. Until when may you keep it?', opts: ['30 days', 'Until the end of its second year', 'It must be eaten that same day'], a: 0,
          e: 'Once twelve months have passed, a newly blemished firstborn may only be kept for thirty more days.' },
      ];
      YC.forEach(() => addMax(1));
      $('yc').innerHTML = YC.map((y, i) => `
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#3a3122] bg-[#1d1912] p-4">
          <p>${y.q}</p>
          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-2">${y.opts.map((o, j) => `<button class="chip text-sm" data-y="${i}" data-o="${j}">${o}</button>`).join('')}</div>
          <div id="yc-fb-${i}"></div>
        </div>`).join('');
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-y]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const i = +b.dataset.y, y = YC[i], ok = +b.dataset.o === y.a;
        document.querySelectorAll(`[data-y="${i}"]`).forEach((x) => { x.disabled = true; if (+x.dataset.o === y.a) x.classList.add('good'); });
        if (!ok) b.classList.add('bad'); else award(1);
        $(`yc-fb-${i}`).innerHTML = note(ok, `${y.e} ${ref('Bekhorot.26b.9', '26b:9')}`);
      }));

      /* ---------- 3. Rava's board ---------- */
      const STATES = ['Disputed', 'All permit', 'All forbid'];
      const STYLE = ['!text-[#d9b45a]', '!text-[#8fae7a]', '!text-[#c0664a]'];
      const RV = [
        { who: 'First tanna', sub: 'Akavya and the Rabbis argue about the dead animal, and about the slaughtered one too. He says “died” to show how far Akavya goes.', ans: [0, 0] },
        { who: 'Rabbi Yehuda', sub: 'His version of the dispute matches the mishna in Eduyot 5:6.', ans: [0, 2] },
        { who: 'Rabbi Yosei', sub: 'His father Ḥalafta conceded to Akavya in one case.', ans: [1, 0] },
      ];
      addMax(3);
      const rvState = RV.map(() => [-1, -1]);
      let rvDone = false;
      $('rv-body').innerHTML = RV.map((r, i) => `
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left align-top font-bold !text-[#efe7d6] pr-2">${r.who}</th>
          ${[0, 1].map((j) => `<td><button class="chip w-full text-sm" data-r="${i}" data-c="${j}" aria-label="${r.who}, ${j ? 'died' : 'slaughtered'}">?</button></td>`).join('')}
        </tr>`).join('');
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-r]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (rvDone) return;
        const i = +b.dataset.r, j = +b.dataset.c;
        rvState[i][j] = (rvState[i][j] + 1) % 3;
        b.className = `chip w-full text-sm ${STYLE[rvState[i][j]]}`;
        b.textContent = STATES[rvState[i][j]];
      }));
      $('rv-check').addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (rvDone) return;
        if (rvState.some((r) => r.includes(-1))) { $('rv-out').innerHTML = note(false, 'Fill in all six cells first.'); return; }
        rvDone = true; $('rv-check').disabled = true;
        let rows = 0;
        RV.forEach((r, i) => {
          const ok = r.ans.every((a, j) => rvState[i][j] === a);
          if (ok) rows++;
          [0, 1].forEach((j) => {
            const b = document.querySelector(`[data-r="${i}"][data-c="${j}"]`);
            b.disabled = true;
            b.classList.add(rvState[i][j] === r.ans[j] ? 'good' : 'bad');
            if (rvState[i][j] !== r.ans[j]) b.textContent = `${STATES[rvState[i][j]]} → ${STATES[r.ans[j]]}`;
          });
        });
        award(rows);
        $('rv-out').innerHTML = note(rows === 3, `${rows} of 3 tannaim right. ${RV.map((r) => `<br><b>${r.who}:</b> ${r.sub}`).join('')}
          <br><br>The Gemara first thought Rabbi Yosei was arguing with the first tanna over Reish Lakish’s requirement that an expert permit the animal before the wool falls. Rava: no. Everyone requires the expert, and these are three separate disputes. Rav Naḥman: the halakha follows Rabbi Yehuda. ${ref('Bekhorot.26a.4-8', '26a:4–8')}`);
      });

      /* ---------- 4. Suspects ---------- */
      const SUS = [
        { t: 'Rabbi Yosei · slaughtered', fits: false, e: 'For Rabbi Yosei, everyone permits wool once the animal is slaughtered. Then both kinds of dangling wool would be permitted, with no difference between them.' },
        { t: 'Rabbi Yosei · died · the Rabbis', fits: false, e: 'The Rabbis forbid wool from an animal that died, so both kinds would be forbidden.' },
        { t: 'Rabbi Yosei · died · Akavya', fits: false, e: 'Akavya would rule the other way round. Wool that looks like part of the fleece was still attached at death, so it’s forbidden. Wool that doesn’t was already detached, so it’s permitted. That’s the reverse of the mishna.' },
        { t: 'Rabbi Yehuda · died', fits: false, e: 'For Rabbi Yehuda, everyone forbids wool from an animal that died, so both kinds would be forbidden.' },
        { t: 'Rabbi Yehuda · slaughtered · Akavya', fits: false, e: 'Akavya permits even shed wool once the animal is slaughtered, so both kinds would be permitted.' },
        { t: 'Rabbi Yehuda · slaughtered · the Rabbis', fits: true, e: 'Yes. The Rabbis forbid wool that came off before slaughter, but wool still attached is permitted when it’s shorn after slaughter. Wool that looks like part of the fleece counts as attached, and wool that doesn’t counts as already shed. So Akavya and the Rabbis disagree about a <i>slaughtered</i> animal, just as Rabbi Yehuda said. “Conclude from it that this is so.”' },
      ];
      addMax(SUS.length);
      let susLeft = SUS.length, susScore = 0;
      $('sus').innerHTML = SUS.map((s, i) => `
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#3a3122] bg-[#1d1912] p-3" id="sus-${i}">
          <p class="font-bold">${s.t}</p>
          <div class="mt-2 flex gap-2">
            <button class="chip text-sm" data-s="${i}" data-v="1">Fits</button>
            <button class="chip text-sm" data-s="${i}" data-v="0">Doesn’t fit</button>
          </div>
          <div id="sus-fb-${i}"></div>
        </div>`).join('');
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-s]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const i = +b.dataset.s, s = SUS[i], ok = (b.dataset.v === '1') === s.fits;
        document.querySelectorAll(`[data-s="${i}"]`).forEach((x) => { x.disabled = true; if ((x.dataset.v === '1') === s.fits) x.classList.add('good'); });
        if (!ok) b.classList.add('bad'); else { award(1); susScore++; }
        if (!s.fits) $(`sus-${i}`).classList.add('opacity-70');
        $(`sus-fb-${i}`).innerHTML = note(ok, s.e);
        if (--susLeft === 0) $('sus-out').innerHTML = note(true, `${susScore} of ${SUS.length} suspects ruled correctly. Only one survives: the clause is the Rabbis’ view in a slaughtered animal, which proves Rabbi Yehuda’s version of the dispute. ${ref('Bekhorot.26a.12-13', '26a:12–13')}`);
      }));

      /* ---------- 5. Fleece press ---------- */
      // up: root turned outward (toward the tip); loose: doesn't press down with the fleece
      const STR = [
        { x: 60, up: false, loose: false }, { x: 105, up: true, loose: false }, { x: 150, up: false, loose: true },
        { x: 195, up: true, loose: true }, { x: 240, up: false, loose: false }, { x: 285, up: false, loose: true },
        { x: 330, up: false, loose: false }, { x: 375, up: true, loose: false }, { x: 420, up: false, loose: true },
        { x: 465, up: false, loose: false }, { x: 510, up: true, loose: false }, { x: 550, up: false, loose: false },
      ];
      const LENSES = [
        { name: 'Reish Lakish', test: (s) => s.up },
        { name: 'Rav Natan bar Oshaya', test: (s) => s.loose },
      ];
      addMax(LENSES.length * 2 + 1);
      let flLens = 0, flPressed = false;
      const flMarked = new Set();
      const drawFleece = () => {
        const svg = $('fl-svg');
        let h = `<rect x="0" y="160" width="600" height="60" fill="#3a3122" />`;
        for (let i = 0; i < 26; i++) h += `<circle cx="${i * 24 + 6}" cy="${162 + (i % 2) * 6}" r="16" fill="#e4dac4" />`;
        h += `<g id="fl-plate" class="press-plate" style="transform: translateY(${flPressed ? 92 : 0}px)"><rect x="10" y="4" width="580" height="12" rx="4" fill="#7a6542" /><rect x="290" y="0" width="20" height="8" fill="#7a6542" /></g>`;
        STR.forEach((s, i) => {
          const len = 100 + (i % 3) * 14, top = 158 - len;
          const sw = (i % 2 ? 10 : -10);
          const path = `M${s.x} 158 C ${s.x + sw} ${158 - len * 0.4}, ${s.x - sw} ${158 - len * 0.7}, ${s.x + sw / 2} ${top}`;
          const rootY = s.up ? top : 156, rootX = s.up ? s.x + sw / 2 : s.x;
          const marked = flMarked.has(i);
          h += `<g class="strand ${s.loose ? '' : 'flat'}" data-i="${i}" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-pressed="${marked}" aria-label="Strand ${i + 1}${s.up ? ', root turned outward' : ''}">
            <path d="${path}" stroke="transparent" stroke-width="22" fill="none" />
            <path d="${path}" stroke="${marked ? '#c0664a' : '#f4ecdb'}" stroke-width="${marked ? 5 : 4}" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" />
            <circle cx="${rootX}" cy="${rootY}" r="5" fill="#d9b45a" />
          </g>`;
        });
        svg.innerHTML = h;
        svg.classList.toggle('pressed', flPressed);
        svg.querySelectorAll('.strand').forEach((g) => {
          const tog = () => {
            const i = +g.dataset.i;
            flMarked.has(i) ? flMarked.delete(i) : flMarked.add(i);
            drawFleece();
            const again = svg.querySelector(`.strand[data-i="${i}"]`); if (again) again.focus();
          };
          g.addEventListener('click', tog);
          g.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => { if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') { e.preventDefault(); tog(); } });
        });
      };
      $('fl-press').addEventListener('click', () => {
        flPressed = !flPressed;
        $('fl-press').textContent = flPressed ? 'Lift the press ⤒' : 'Press the fleece ⤓';
        drawFleece();
      });
      $('fl-check').addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (flLens >= LENSES.length) return;
        const L = LENSES[flLens];
        const want = new Set(STR.map((s, i) => (L.test(s) ? i : -1)).filter((i) => i >= 0));
        const exact = want.size === flMarked.size && [...want].every((i) => flMarked.has(i));
        const hits = [...flMarked].filter((i) => want.has(i)).length;
        const pts = exact ? 2 : hits >= want.size - 1 && flMarked.size <= want.size + 1 ? 1 : 0;
        award(pts);
        let msg = `${exact ? 'Exactly right.' : `You needed ${want.size} strands. ${hits} of your ${flMarked.size} were right.`} `;
        msg += L.name === 'Reish Lakish'
          ? 'Reish Lakish only forbids strands whose root is turned outward, the gold dot at the tip. The press doesn’t matter to him.'
          : 'Rav Natan bar Oshaya forbids the strands that spring back up when you press, whichever way their root faces.';
        flLens++;
        flMarked.clear();
        if (flLens < LENSES.length) {
          $('fl-lens').textContent = LENSES[flLens].name;
          msg += ' Now rule the same fleece by <b>Rav Natan bar Oshaya</b>.';
          $('fl-out').innerHTML = note(exact, msg);
        } else {
          $('fl-lens').textContent = 'done';
          $('fl-check').disabled = true;
          $('fl-out').innerHTML = note(exact, msg) + `
            <p class="mt-4">Rav Natan’s reading is the plain meaning of “doesn’t look like part of the fleece”. Why didn’t Reish Lakish say it?</p>
            <div class="mt-2 grid gap-2">
              <button class="chip text-sm" data-ile="0">Because the root decides whether a hair grows from the animal</button>
              <button class="chip text-sm" data-ile="1">Because no fleece is without a few loose hairs, so under Rav Natan none of it could ever be used</button>
              <button class="chip text-sm" data-ile="2">Because Reish Lakish follows Akavya ben Mahalalel</button>
            </div><div id="ile-fb"></div>`;
          document.querySelectorAll('[data-ile]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
            const ok = b.dataset.ile === '1';
            document.querySelectorAll('[data-ile]').forEach((x) => { x.disabled = true; if (x.dataset.ile === '1') x.classList.add('good'); });
            if (!ok) b.classList.add('bad'); else award(1);
            $('ile-fb').innerHTML = note(ok, `Rabbi Ile’a: “it is impossible for there to be fleece without dangling hairs.” If every strand that doesn’t press down were forbidden, the fleece of a dead firstborn could never be used, so Reish Lakish reads the mishna more leniently. ${ref('Bekhorot.26b.6', '26b:6')}`);
          }));
        }
        drawFleece();
      });
      drawFleece();

      /* ---------- 6. Yannai's shelf ---------- */
      const SHELF = ['Permitted', 'Forbidden', 'This is the question'];
      const YN = [
        { t: '🐐 Sin offering', a: 0, e: 'It comes to atone, so the owner won’t keep it longer than he has to. No reason to forbid the wool.' },
        { t: '🐏 Guilt offering', a: 0, e: 'Also brought for atonement, and offered quickly. No question.' },
        { t: '🐑 Firstborn', a: 1, e: 'It doesn’t atone, so an owner might keep it around. The wool is forbidden so he won’t be tempted to shear it or work it.' },
        { t: '🐄 Animal tithe', a: 1, e: 'Like the firstborn, it doesn’t atone and might be kept. Forbidden.' },
        { t: '🔥 Burnt offering', a: 2, e: 'This is Rabbi Yannai’s dilemma. Atonement isn’t its main purpose, so maybe he keeps it. But it does atone for neglecting a positive mitzva, so maybe he doesn’t.' },
      ];
      addMax(YN.length + 1);
      let ynLeft = YN.length;
      $('yn').innerHTML = YN.map((y, i) => `
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#3a3122] bg-[#1d1912] p-3">
          <p class="font-bold">${y.t}</p>
          <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-2">${SHELF.map((s, j) => `<button class="chip text-sm" data-yn="${i}" data-o="${j}">${s}</button>`).join('')}</div>
          <div id="yn-fb-${i}"></div>
        </div>`).join('');
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-yn]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const i = +b.dataset.yn, y = YN[i], ok = +b.dataset.o === y.a;
        document.querySelectorAll(`[data-yn="${i}"]`).forEach((x) => { x.disabled = true; if (+x.dataset.o === y.a) x.classList.add('good'); });
        if (!ok) b.classList.add('bad'); else award(1);
        $(`yn-fb-${i}`).innerHTML = note(ok, `${y.e} ${ref('Bekhorot.26a.15', '26a:15')}`);
        if (--ynLeft === 0) showProof();
      }));
      const showProof = () => {
        $('yn-proof').innerHTML = `
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#4a4232] bg-[#211c14] p-4">
            <p class="text-sm !text-[#a59a83]">Come and hear (${ref('Bekhorot.26b.2-4', '26b:2–4')})</p>
            <p class="mt-2">The baraita: “One who <b>plucks</b> the wool from an unblemished firstborn, even if it later got a blemish and was slaughtered, may not use it.” So wool that fell by itself from a firstborn is permitted, and a burnt offering’s even more so? The Gemara rejects the proof. Why does the baraita say “plucks”?</p>
            <div class="mt-3 grid gap-2">
              <button class="chip text-sm" data-pf="0">Because the baraita is only about wool someone pulled out on purpose</button>
              <button class="chip text-sm" data-pf="1">To match its second clause, where Akavya permits a blemished animal’s wool even when it was plucked</button>
              <button class="chip text-sm" data-pf="2">Because wool that fell out never belongs to the kohen</button>
            </div><div id="pf-fb"></div>
          </div>`;
        document.querySelectorAll('[data-pf]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const ok = b.dataset.pf === '1';
          document.querySelectorAll('[data-pf]').forEach((x) => { x.disabled = true; if (x.dataset.pf === '1') x.classList.add('good'); });
          if (!ok) b.classList.add('bad'); else award(1);
          $('pf-fb').innerHTML = note(ok, 'Shed wool from an unblemished firstborn really is forbidden too. The baraita says “plucks” because its second clause does: there Akavya permits a blemished firstborn’s wool even when it was plucked, which shows how far he goes. The mishna says “shed” for the opposite reason, to show how far the Rabbis go: they forbid even wool that just fell. So the proof fails, and the daf moves on without resolving Rabbi Yannai’s question.');
        }));
      };

      /* ---------- 7. Threshing floor ---------- */
      const TF = [
        { q: 'Kohanim, Levites and poor people help out at the shepherd’s house, the threshing floor and the slaughterhouse. The owner pays them with teruma and tithes. What has he done?', opts: ['Nothing wrong. They are entitled to it anyway', 'He has desecrated the sacred gifts', 'The gifts are void and go back to being untithed'], a: 1,
          e: '“If one did so, he desecrated” (חִילְּלוּ). Malachi 2:8 is said about them: “you have corrupted the covenant of Levi.”' },
        { q: 'The baraita adds a second verse, Numbers 18:32: “and you shall not desecrate the sacred items… that you shall not die.” Why add it?', opts: ['To show this is a sin, not just a desecration of the produce', 'To teach that Levites are included', 'To give the source for the fifty days'], a: 0,
          e: 'You might think the first verse only means the teruma is desecrated. The second verse adds a punishment of death at the hands of Heaven.' },
        { q: 'The Sages wanted to fine such owners by making them separate teruma again. Why didn’t they?', opts: ['The kohen had already eaten it', 'People might think the produce was never tithed and tithe from exempt produce for produce that still owes tithes', 'Fines can’t be imposed on teruma'], a: 1,
          e: 'By Torah law the produce was already tithed. Someone who saw it tithed again might use it to tithe other produce that still owes tithes, so the fine would cause a worse mistake.' },
      ];
      TF.forEach(() => addMax(1));
      $('tf').innerHTML = TF.map((t, i) => `
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#3a3122] bg-[#1d1912] p-4">
          <p>${t.q}</p>
          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-2">${t.opts.map((o, j) => `<button class="chip text-sm" data-tf="${i}" data-o="${j}">${o}</button>`).join('')}</div>
          <div id="tf-fb-${i}"></div>
        </div>`).join('');
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-tf]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const i = +b.dataset.tf, t = TF[i], ok = +b.dataset.o === t.a;
        document.querySelectorAll(`[data-tf="${i}"]`).forEach((x) => { x.disabled = true; if (+x.dataset.o === t.a) x.classList.add('good'); });
        if (!ok) b.classList.add('bad'); else award(1);
        $(`tf-fb-${i}`).innerHTML = note(ok, `${t.e} ${ref('Bekhorot.26b.18-20', '26b:18–20')}`);
      }));
    })();
  </script>
</Layout>
